- op: discuss  # 080b
  at: '2026-10-19T07:16:00Z'  # 080b
  by: agent  # 080b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 080b
  clock: 3  # 080b
  nonce: 080b  # 080b
  message: "Fixed in PR #1726 (dev 2fc12de026).\n\nBehavioral evidence: the item's own repro, re-run on merged dev through analyze_scala / analyze_kotlin:\n  scala  Runtime.getRuntime.availableProcessors  -> scala:java.lang.Runtime:0-0:getRuntime + scala:java.lang.Runtime:0-0:availableProcessors  (was: no edge)\n  scala  System.currentTimeMillis (no parens)    -> scala:java.lang.System:0-0:currentTimeMillis  (was: no edge)\n  scala  System.currentTimeMillis() (control)    -> same dst, unchanged\n  kotlin Runtime.getRuntime().exec(c).inputStream -> kotlin:java.lang.Process:0-0:getInputStream  (was: no edge)\n  kotlin ...getInputStream() (control)            -> same dst, unchanged\ncatalogue lookup_with_module(call_construct=method): Runtime.availableProcessors and System.currentTimeMillis -> host_info_read, scala.io.StdIn.readLine -> ipc_recv.\n\nFix: the grammar cannot tell a parameterless call from a field read (System.out), so a member access with no argument list counts as a call ONLY where a library-signature row or a function/method io_primitives row says the owner declares that method (jvm_implicit_imports.is_known_library_method). Kotlin tries getX / isX, and an isX property's own name; a getter's returned type (signature row) is the next link's owner.\n\nCorpus, calls edges vs dev: sbt +150, gatling +7, okhttp +1, detekt 0; 0 lost in all four. The named sites gatling ActorSystem.scala:36 and sbt EvaluateTask.scala:223 now emit getRuntime + availableProcessors.\n\nScope NOT covered: a PROJECT parameterless def called without parens (only library rows count); a library method no row names; and a receiver declared with a bare java.lang type, filed as INV-dibij (scala's call arm leaves p.getInputStream() external while the new parameterless arm qualifies the same receiver; kotlin v(p: Process) = p.inputStream emits nothing)."  # 080b
